audioconvert, stream: replay info only to listeners that take it

A full emit of a node's info toggles the SERIAL flag of every param with
a change pending and clears the change. add_listener replays that full
emit to the listener being added, isolated from the rest, and
spa_node_enum_params_sync adds a listener that takes results alone, so
each synchronous enumeration of the converter used up a pending Props
change that no real listener heard. With one swallowed, the converter's
next change, a mute say, toggles SERIAL back to the value the adapter
already holds; the adapter sees no change, emits nothing, and clients
keep the old value until something else changes. audioadapter.c already
replays only to a listener with info or port_info.

--- a/spa/plugins/audioconvert/audioconvert.c
+++ b/spa/plugins/audioconvert/audioconvert.c
@@ -2661,7 +2661,12 @@
 	spa_log_trace(this->log, "%p: add listener %p", this, listener);
 	spa_hook_list_isolate(&this->hooks, &save, listener, events, data);
 
-	emit_info(this, true);
+	/* Only replay info to listeners that take it. A full emit toggles the
+	 * SERIAL bit of pending params and clears their user count; doing that
+	 * for a result-only listener (spa_node_*_enum_params_sync) silently
+	 * consumes a pending change that the real listeners never see. */
+	if (events->info || events->port_info)
+		emit_info(this, true);
 
 	spa_hook_list_join(&this->hooks, &save);
 
--- a/src/pipewire/stream.c
+++ b/src/pipewire/stream.c
@@ -748,8 +748,12 @@
 
 	spa_hook_list_isolate(&d->hooks, &save, listener, events, data);
 
-	emit_node_info(d, true);
-	emit_port_info(d, true);
+	/* As in audioconvert: don't consume pending SERIAL toggles for
+	 * result-only listeners. */
+	if (events->info)
+		emit_node_info(d, true);
+	if (events->port_info)
+		emit_port_info(d, true);
 
 	spa_hook_list_join(&d->hooks, &save);
 
